{
  "bead_id": "B-b490acff",
  "title": "Tighten fraction regex to match spec exactly",
  "agent_type": "developer",
  "description": "The current fraction parser in CookbookCore is more permissive than the spec's value-resolution rules. The spec at specs/planned/0001-cooklang-parser.md (section 'Quantity parsing semantics') defines the fraction pattern as exactly: ^\\d+\\s*/\\s*[1-9]\\d*$ \u2014 meaning the numerator is a non-negative integer (no minus sign), and the denominator is a positive integer that does NOT start with 0. The current implementation deviates by accepting cases like '-1/2' (negative numerator) and '1/0' (zero denominator), parsing them as numbers when they should fall through to the .text(...) value branch. This is a foundational data type \u2014 every recipe view, every shopping-list aggregation reads Quantity values directly \u2014 so the parser must conform to the spec exactly, with no permissiveness drift.",
  "status": "done",
  "bead_type": "task",
  "parent_id": "B-2dfeba7e",
  "dependencies": [],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "The fraction-detection regex (or equivalent matcher) in Packages/CookbookCore/Sources/CookbookCore/Parser.swift matches exactly ^\\d+\\s*/\\s*[1-9]\\d*$ \u2014 non-negative integer numerator, positive integer denominator with no leading zero.",
    "Parsing '@x{-1/2%cup}' produces Quantity(value: .text(\"-1/2\"), unit: \"cup\") (NOT .number(-0.5)).",
    "Parsing '@x{1/0%cup}' produces Quantity(value: .text(\"1/0\"), unit: \"cup\") (NOT .number) \u2014 zero denominator falls through to text branch.",
    "Parsing '@x{1/02%cup}' produces Quantity(value: .text(\"1/02\"), unit: \"cup\") (NOT .number) \u2014 leading-zero denominator falls through to text branch.",
    "Parsing '@x{0/2%cup}' produces Quantity(value: .number(0.0), unit: \"cup\") \u2014 zero numerator IS valid per spec (\\d+ matches 0).",
    "Existing valid-fraction cases continue to pass: '@x{1/2%cup}' \u2192 .number(0.5), '@x{3 / 4%cup}' \u2192 .number(0.75).",
    "New @Test functions added to CooklangParserTests.swift cover all 4 invalid cases above (-1/2, 1/0, 1/02) and the 0/2 valid case.",
    "swift test from Packages/CookbookCore/ passes with all tests green (existing 54 + the new ones)."
  ],
  "linked_docs": [
    "specs/planned/0001-cooklang-parser.md"
  ],
